	(text "Beacon: the MCU sends 38 kHz NEC frames (TIM1 PWM, ~1/3 duty), never a steady carrier:\nthe robot receivers (IRM-H638T) suppress continuous 38 kHz. Left and right strings can send\ndifferent codes. Gates are AC-coupled (100 nF / 100k, ~10 ms): a pin stuck high turns the LEDs off.\nMount the three LEDs of each string fanned out (IR204C-A-L, 3 mm, is +/-20 deg) to cover the room.\nPulsed overdrive (2026-11-24): 2x 150R per string = 75R, ~210 mA peak (IR204C-A-L: 100 mA DC,\n1 A at <= 100 us / 1 %; the carrier is ~9 us at 1/3). Fit only R1004/R1006 for ~100 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fdeab193-7c0a-4dd3-9795-ae6fc60ed8e8")
	)
